{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And every firstborn donkey.</b> Since it is impure, you shall redeem with a lamb." "<b>And you shall break its neck.</b> Some say: write 'holy' upon its neck. And one who says thus, I say that he is a stubborn donkey, for it is written הוא יערוף מזבחותיהם (Hosea 10:2), and וערפו שם את העגלה בנחל (Deuteronomy 21:4), whose meaning is to cut the neck, as the translators of the Law interpreted. For every firstborn that is not brought near the altar or is not redeemed is liable to death, for every firstborn of Egypt, man and beast, died; for HaShem did not spare them from the decree that He decreed upon the firstborn of Egypt, but only that they be set apart for His service. And Israel had no impure beasts except donkeys alone; therefore a firstborn is not redeemed with another species."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "'קדש על ערפו' understood as inscribing 'holy' on the animal's neck; the whole passage is cited as the opinion Ibn Ezra rejects."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:11.565587207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}